# Miner Llama v4 preset: Flint, Flint Pascal Q8 GGUF (p065) on nine P106-090 cards, 262,144-token context.
# Build: v4-rc2 (pascal-p106-v4 eb82916d3, upstream b12360 merged). On it this file loads with the same memory on
# every card and gives the same greedy replies as before the upstream merge (docs/data/2026-11-13_c831_upstream/,
# part 3). Its agent check against v3.0 is the release test in README.md; v3.0 on this file and line: 47.4 tok/s,
# 12/12 (docs/data/2026-11-05_release_regression/).
# This is v3.0's line (release/flint-v3/settings.env) with the v4 switches that act on Flint's path: host-side,
# exact (the same tokens), and checked on nine P106 cards. Flint's file holds Q8_0 and Q5_0 weights, F16 routers and
# F32 norms; Flint decodes one token a step, its pipelined guesses too, so the v4 kernels of 2-8-token verify passes
# never run here (README.md, "What v4 changes").
# Use: . settings.env && env $PRESET_ENV llama-server -m "$MODELS/$PRESET_MODEL" $PRESET_ARGS --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8080
PRESET_MODEL=flint-pascal-Q8.gguf

PRESET_ENV=
PRESET_ENV="$PRESET_ENV LLAMA_KV_SEQ_RM_BOUND=1"  # removing a sequence's positions visits only the cells it can change, the same cells and head: each dropped pipelined guess no longer sweeps all 262,144 cells (C740, Q1309; R122: -0.33 ms a step on Flash-Next)
PRESET_ENV="$PRESET_ENV LLAMA_SERVER_YIELD=2"  # a step's yield to the server's reader thread wakes it only when a read waits, the same replies (C741, Q1310; R122)
PRESET_ENV="$PRESET_ENV LLAMA_SAMPLING_TOP_K_ROWS=1"  # the card's sampling chain (-bs, top-k 20) runs one top-k over its output rows and reads the logits unpadded, the same tokens (C691, Q1223; R83; the graph fixed by C802, Q1406)
PRESET_ENV=${PRESET_ENV# }

# v3.0's line, unchanged; every flag is explained in release/flint-v3/README.md:
PRESET_ARGS="--alias flint -ngl 99 -fa on -c 262144 -np 1 -b 512 -ub 128 -ts 6,6,5,5,6,5,5,6,6 -bs --ctx-checkpoints 4 --cache-ram 0 --temp 1.0 --top-p 0.95 --top-k 20 --min-p 0 --pipe-depth 4"
